Boards that select the GXL glue variant never run usb3_init(), so the glue's
USB_R1_U3H_HOST_PORT_POWER_CONTROL_PRESENT bit stays clear and HCC_PPC reads 0
even though the controller really does switch port power.

Measured on this board: vendor firmware reports hcc_params 0x0228fe6c
(PPC = 1) while mainline reports 0x0228fe64 (PPC = 0). The only difference is
bit 3, HCC_PPC.

Raise PPC for a platform that opts in with "amlogic,port-power-control",
without writing the glue register (which faults on this board).

--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci.c
@@ -5473,6 +5473,16 @@
 	xhci->hcc_params = readl(&xhci->cap_regs->hcc_params);
 	if (xhci->hci_version > 0x100)
 		xhci->hcc_params2 = readl(&xhci->cap_regs->hcc_params2);
+	/*
+	 * Boards that select the GXL glue variant never run usb3_init(), so the
+	 * glue's PORT_POWER_CONTROL_PRESENT bit stays clear and HCC_PPC reads 0
+	 * although the controller does switch port power; vendor firmware on
+	 * this board reports PPC = 1. Raise it here instead of writing the glue
+	 * register, which faults on this board.
+	 */
+	if (dev->of_node &&
+	    of_property_read_bool(dev->of_node, "amlogic,port-power-control"))
+		xhci->hcc_params |= (1 << 3);
 
 	xhci->dma_mask_bits = 64;
 	xhci->max_slots = HCS_MAX_SLOTS(hcs_params1);
